  "question": "If the projection of the vector $\\vec{a} = 3\\hat{i} + t\\hat{j} + 4\\hat{k}$ on $\\vec{b} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}$ is $2$, find the value(s) of $t$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "Projection of $\\vec{a}$ on $\\vec{b}$ is $\\dfrac{\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}}{|\\vec{b}|}$.<br /><br />$\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}=3(1)+t(2)+4(-2)=3+2t-8=2t-5$.<br /><br />$|\\vec{b}|=\\sqrt{1^2+2^2+(-2)^2}=3$.<br /><br />So $\\dfrac{2t-5}{3}=2$.<br /><br />$2t-5=6 \\Rightarrow 2t=11 \\Rightarrow t=5.5$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
